 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+The error-handling property below remains outside the scope of the usage accounting change in #93.
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+
+## Turn usage accounting (#93)
+
+The chosen contract retains a single summed usage argument for billing and budgeting; a per-round breakdown was rejected because it adds public API surface without being needed for turn totals. The hook signature must identify this argument as total turn usage, and the release must carry a MINOR bump and a changelog entry explaining that existing consumers record larger totals on tool turns.
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once after the round loop and receives the fieldwise sum of usage from every provider call in the turn, including both tool rounds and the final answer ([validated by: reports the sum of all three provider calls after two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L68)).
+- Missing usage on any round is ignored when summing reported rounds; no reporting rounds yields `undefined`, while reported zero counts remain zero ([validated by: sums reported rounds across missing usage and preserves absence when none report](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L78)).
+- A turn with no tool calls retains its existing response text and usage value ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
